WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.348
The dead tiger lay at Mowgli's feet.

2
00:00:05.349 --> 00:00:10.682
"We must work fast," Mowgli said to Akela and Gray Brother.

3
00:00:10.683 --> 00:00:16.504
"I want to lay the tiger's hide at Council Rock."

4
00:00:16.505 --> 00:00:19.383
They got to work preparing the hide.

5
00:00:19.384 --> 00:00:25.879
Suddenly the wolves dashed off, and Mowgli felt a hand clamp down on his shoulder.

6
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.471
Buldeo stood there with his gun.

7
00:00:29.472 --> 00:00:34.838
"That tiger's hide belongs to me!" the hunter growled.

8
00:00:34.839 --> 00:00:37.685
"There's a big reward for it."

9
00:00:37.686 --> 00:00:39.979
Mowgli rolled his eyes.

10
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:45.284
"I'm sure you're planning to give me some of the reward."

11
00:00:45.285 --> 00:00:48.629
"I'm the chief hunter," Buldeo said.

12
00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:52.070
"I'm not going to give you any of the reward.

13
00:00:52.071 --> 00:00:56.844
You caught the tiger only because of dumb luck."

14
00:00:56.845 --> 00:01:01.510
He stooped over Shere Khan, looking at the tiger closely.

15
00:01:01.511 --> 00:01:06.386
"This tiger and I are old enemies," Mowgli said.

16
00:01:06.387 --> 00:01:12.326
Then he waved an arm. "Akela!"

17
00:01:12.327 --> 00:01:16.793
Seconds later Buldeo found himself lying on the grass.

18
00:01:16.794 --> 00:01:19.763
A large gray wolf stood over him.

19
00:01:19.764 --> 00:01:22.316
Buldeo blinked in surprise.

20
00:01:22.317 --> 00:01:25.316
Mowgli had summoned a wolf!

21
00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:29.582
"This is magic of the worst kind!" he thought.

22
00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:33.103
Terrified, he lay as still as a stone.

23
00:01:33.104 --> 00:01:35.570
What if Mowgli summoned more wolves?

24
00:01:35.571 --> 00:01:39.623
Or he turned himself into a wolf or tiger?

25
00:01:39.624 --> 00:01:43.822
"Great King," Buldeo said at last in a whisper.

26
00:01:43.823 --> 00:01:47.100
"Yes?" Mowgli grinned.

27
00:01:47.101 --> 00:01:49.848
Now the hunter was afraid of him.

28
00:01:49.849 --> 00:01:51.631
"I'm an old man.

29
00:01:51.632 --> 00:01:55.211
I didn't know that you were a powerful sorcerer.

30
00:01:55.212 --> 00:02:00.819
May I get up? Will your wolf tear me to pieces?"

31
00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:07.576
"Go. But from now on, leave me alone," Mowgli replied.

32
00:02:07.577 --> 00:02:13.631
"Let him go, Akela," he commanded.

33
00:02:13.632 --> 00:02:18.170
Buldeo limped away to the village as fast as he could.

34
00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:23.896
Every few minutes he looked back nervously.

35
00:02:23.897 --> 00:02:30.565
When he got to the village, he told the villagers about what he'd seen.

36
00:02:30.566 --> 00:02:36.095
Mowgli and the others finished preparing the tiger's hide.

37
00:02:36.096 --> 00:02:40.324
Mowgli hid it near a tree.

38
00:02:40.325 --> 00:02:45.976
Then he gathered the buffalo herd and took them back to the village.

39
00:02:45.977 --> 00:02:49.788
As he approached, bells clanged loudly.

40
00:02:49.789 --> 00:02:54.572
Half the village seemed to be waiting for him by the gate.

41
00:02:54.573 --> 00:03:00.569
"The villagers are happy that I killed the tiger," Mowgli said to himself proudly.

42
00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:05.974
"They must be waiting to thank me!"

43
00:03:05.975 --> 00:03:11.398
Instead a shower of stones whistled past Mowgli's ears.

44
00:03:11.399 --> 00:03:13.723
Angry shouts rose.

45
00:03:13.724 --> 00:03:15.454
"Sorcerer!"

46
00:03:15.455 --> 00:03:17.470
"Jungle demon!"

47
00:03:17.471 --> 00:03:19.872
"Shoot him, Buldeo!"

48
00:03:19.873 --> 00:03:23.191
The old gun went off with a bang.

49
00:03:23.192 --> 00:03:27.897
But the bullet missed Mowgli—striking a buffalo instead.

50
00:03:27.898 --> 00:03:32.101
"The boy just used magic again!" a villager shouted.

51
00:03:32.102 --> 00:03:35.184
"He turned that bullet around with magic!"

52
00:03:35.185 --> 00:03:38.939
The villagers threw more stones at Mowgli.

53
00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.937
He ducked, trying not to panic.

54
00:03:41.938 --> 00:03:45.906
Akela and Gray Brother ran to his sides.

55
00:03:45.907 --> 00:03:50.092
"This is just like the wolf pack," Akela said.

56
00:03:50.093 --> 00:03:53.168
"They want you gone, Mowgli."

57
00:03:53.169 --> 00:04:00.163
"Last time I was told to leave because I'm a human." Mowgli sighed.

58
00:04:00.164 --> 00:04:04.138
"This time it is because I am a wolf!"

59
00:04:04.139 --> 00:04:08.866
Just then Messua ran out from the crowd.

60
00:04:08.867 --> 00:04:14.477
"My son! Are the stories about your magic true?"

61
00:04:14.478 --> 00:04:18.354
Mowgli ducked as more stones whizzed by his head.

62
00:04:18.355 --> 00:04:23.046
"I'm not a sorcerer, Messua. You know that."

63
00:04:23.047 --> 00:04:27.672
"You must go away before they hurt you!" she said.

64
00:04:27.673 --> 00:04:30.940
A few people pumped their fists in the air.

65
00:04:30.941 --> 00:04:34.815
"Get away from the sorcerer, Messua!" they shouted.

66
00:04:34.816 --> 00:04:39.444
"Come back here, or we will stone you too!"

67
00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:42.517
Mowgli quickly hugged Messua.

68
00:04:42.518 --> 00:04:45.555
He thanked her for her kindness to him.

69
00:04:45.556 --> 00:04:53.468
Then he and the two wolves ran away from the people's village.

